#
# Settings derived from the shpack environment. The locations themselves --
# ROOT, STORE, DISTFILES, BUILDDIR, ARCH, BASEPATH and optionally JOBS -- are
# environment variables: the kaem driver (bootstrap/start.kaem) exports them
# after reading shpack.conf, and the test fixture exports them directly. What
# is here follows from $STORE, and each line yields to a value already in the
# environment (the tests set SANDBOX= and PATCH_SHEBANGS= to build
# unsandboxed). Plain POSIX shell, sourced by bin/shpack.

# The tcc/musl bootstrap dash, used ONLY as the dag.mk driver-make shell (the
# top make that runs `shpack build-one` per node). It exists from the first kaem
# package on. Per-build shells are not taken from here: every built recipe
# declares its own dash dep and the builder's $sh follows it -- `depends_on dash`
# for the clean glibc dash, `depends_on dash@0.5.12` for this bootstrap one (an
# external). There is no /bin/sh anywhere, so this is an absolute store path.
CONFIG_SHELL=${CONFIG_SHELL:-$STORE/dash-0.5.12/bin/sh}

# When this spec occurs in a DAG, shpack builds it first, serially, under the
# bootstrap-era make (3.82, whose -j has races), then schedules the rest -jN
# under it.
SHPACK_BOOTSTRAP_MAKE=${SHPACK_BOOTSTRAP_MAKE-gmake@4.4.1}

# The Landlock launcher each build step is wrapped in (kaem phase, built right
# after tcc+musl). Confines a build to the store (read+exec), the recipe tree
# and distfiles (read), and its own prefix plus scratch (write), so the host
# /usr is invisible and stray writes are denied. Empty builds unsandboxed.
SANDBOX=${SANDBOX-$STORE/sandbox-1.0/bin/sandbox}

# Rewrites `#!/bin/sh` shebangs in each unpacked source to the recipe's build
# shell ($sh, its declared dash) before building, since the sandbox has no host
# /bin/sh for install-sh/config.guess and friends. Empty skips it.
PATCH_SHEBANGS=${PATCH_SHEBANGS-$STORE/patch-shebangs-1.0/bin/patch-shebangs}
